From: Marble Kernel Builder <builder@local>
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: arm64: initialize clidr for Clang 22 -Wuninitialized-const-pointer

Clang 22 treats an uninitialized `struct sys_reg_desc clidr` passed to
get_clidr_el1() as an error under -Werror (-Wuninitialized-const-pointer).

get_clidr_el1() fills clidr.val; zero-init is a no-op for runtime and silences
the diagnostic on older Android GKI trees that still use this pattern.

Marble-local: pa-gr/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8450 @ vauxite only.
Remove when upstream includes an equivalent fix or reworks this path.

---
 arch/arm64/kvm/sys_regs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/sys_regs.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/sys_regs.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/sys_regs.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/sys_regs.c
@@ -2750,7 +2750,7 @@ void kvm_sys_reg_table_init(void)
 {
 	unsigned int i;
-	struct sys_reg_desc clidr;
+	struct sys_reg_desc clidr = {0};
 
 	/* Make sure tables are unique and in order. */
 	BUG_ON(check_sysreg_table(sys_reg_descs, ARRAY_SIZE(sys_reg_descs), false));
